{"packet_id": "D067-03", "doc_id": "D067", "jurisdiction": "NJ", "category": "rent_increase_limits", "lifecycle": "enacted", "title": "Rent increases must be conscionable and comply with rent control", "requirement": "A rent increase the tenant refuses to pay supports eviction only if it is not unconscionable and complies with all laws and municipal rent control ordinances; the tenant may withhold the difference while court decides.", "key_value": null, "coverage_conditions": "Residential tenancies subject to the Anti-Eviction Act; the increase must comply with any applicable municipal rent control ordinance.", "applicability": {"built_on_or_before": null, "built_after": null, "date_basis": null, "min_units": null, "max_units": null, "owner_dependent": false, "other": null}, "exemptions": null, "penalty": null, "effective_date": null, "citation": "N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1(f)", "quoted_span": "If a tenant fails to pay rent after being given notice of a rent increase and a Notice to Quit,
